Query the following two values from the STATION table:

The sum of all values in LAT_N rounded to a scale of  decimal places.
The sum of all values in LONG_W rounded to a scale of  decimal places.
Input Format

The STATION table is described as follows:

SELECT ROUND(SUM(LAT_N), 2), ROUND(SUM(LONG_W), 2)
FROM STATION;


SUM(LAT_N) and SUM(LONG_W): These are aggregate functions that calculate the total of all values in the LAT_N (Northern Latitude) and LONG_W (Western Longitude) columns across every row in the STATION table.
ROUND(..., 2): The ROUND function takes the resulting sums and limits them to 2 decimal places.
Example: If the sum is 42850.038, ROUND(..., 2) will return 42850.04.
FROM STATION: This specifies the source table containing the data. 
Expected Output
The query returns a single row with two values: 
The rounded sum of all latitudes.
The rounded sum of all longitudes. 
ROUND(SUM(LAT_N), 2) 	ROUND(SUM(LONG_W), 2)
42850.04	47381.48
